{"url": "https://melamoracollege.com/department-of-political-science-2/", "retrieved": "2026-10-02", "status": "ok", "final_url": "https://melamoracollege.com/department-of-political-science-2/", "text": "Department of Political Science – MELAMORA COLLEGE\nHave any questions?\nadmin@melamoracollege.com\nOffice Login\nFaculty Login\nStudent Login\nHome\nAbout us\nOur Vision & Mission\nCode of conduct:\nProfessional Ethics\nCore Values\nSWOC of Melamora College\nInstitutional Distinctiveness\nBest practice\nAcademic\nAdmission Procedure\nCourse\nADD-ON COURSE\nB.A 1st Semester (FYUGP) 2024-25 Session\nProgramme Outcome\nHoliday List\nAcademic calender\nFee Structure\nFreeship and Scholarships\nRegulations\nGuidelines Reservation Policy of the Government\nReservation Policy\nProspectus\nClass Routine\nFacilities\nLIBRARY\nAdministrations\nGoverning Body\nPrincipal\nVice Principal\nTeaching Staff\nNon- Teaching Staff\nOffice Staff\nLibrary Staff\nOrganogram of the institution\nDepartments\nDepartment of Political Science\nDepartment of Economics\nDepartment of Sociology\nDepartment of English\nDepartment of Philosophy\nDepartment of Assamese\nDepartment of Education\nDepartment of History\nStudent Corner\nCollege-Magazine\nUnion Body\nAlumni\nAnti Ragging Committee\nConstitution of the Melamora College Student’s union\nExtension Cell\nIQAC Minutes\nIQAC ACTIVITIES\nCells And Committees\nInstitutional policy\nAction Taken Report\nAchievements\nAcademic Achievements\nSports and Other Achievements\nIQAC\nSSR\nDVV  Clarifications\n1 st CYCLE SSR\nAQAR\nNIRF\nPhoto Gallery\nNAAC Peer Team Visit\nDownload\nNew Voter Registration\nDEPARTMENTAL PROFILE\nPOLITICAL SCIENCE DEPARTMENT\nDesk From Head of the Department\nMr. Luhit Nath\nH.O.D., Political Science\nPersonal Profile\nThe department of Political Science was established in the year 1987 with the inception of the College. Political Science has gradually evolved into a discipline which encompasses a study not only domestic Politics but also international political scenario. moreover, the inter disciplinary character of the discipline makes the subject a very interesting field of study .it offers the students many opportunities for career building and intellectual avenue as well.\nCOURSE OFFERED:\nB.A.Honours in Political Science, (In CBCS Mode)\nB.A. General in Political Science, (In CBCS Mode)\nVISION\n:\nTo bring an overall improvement in the society by imparting quality higher education (value based and skill based education).\nTo make our students responsible, knowledgeable and competent citizens of society.\nMISSION\nThe Department of Political Science was started with a mission to impart quality higher education for all sections of society especially to the socially,economically,and educationally disadvantaged students of rural areas and TGL(Tea Garden Labours) communities. We aspire to equip students for life, making them not only competent job seekers but also to be self-employed socially committed citizens well equipped with a sense of tolerance and justice by making them aware of their rights and duties for the betterment of the society.\nTo create an academic environment for promotion of quality education.\nTo arrange for periodic assessment of students’ progression and development.\nTo promote quality research and innovative practices.\nTo work together with the other stake holders for quality evaluation, promotion and sustenance.\nABOUT THE DEPARTMENT :\nThe prestigious Dept of Political Science of this College was established in the year 1987.As a discipline of Arts, Political Science Dept has been offering honours & non honours courses .The objectives of the dept are\nTo impart theoretical & empirical understanding of the subject to its student\nTo help the students pursue their higher education in political Science.\nTo promote research endeavors of the faculty for better understanding of issues of political significance in India.\nSTRENGTH :\nOne of the oldest department in this College & many pass students are now working in different Schools and Colleges and other sectors.\nEfficient, sincere & hard working faculties.\nPromoting students performance.\nUses of technical and innovative methods in teaching.\nActive faulty involvement in student related programmes.\nDOWNOLAD\nNoticication\nResult\nSylabus\nAcademic Calendar\nHoliday\nList\nMerit List\nCourse Structure\nCBCS\nDEPARTMENTAL\nLIBRARY\nhttps://youtu.be/tKq5aCaVcSA\nINNOVATIVE PRACTICE:\nU\nsing ICT tools like smart classroom, google meet ,zoom,google classroom,whats app group etc.\nP\nower point presentation\nP\naper presentation\nIINFRASTRUCTURAL FACILITIES:\nLIBRARY\n:The central library of the College is the general need of the students. However,the Dept also has a reference library with total no of 100 books.\nWALL MAGAZINE:\nA hand written wall magazine “VANGUARD” is published every year.\nCOMPUTER :\nPersonal Laptop is used in departmental activities.\nENRICHMENT\nOF\nCOURSE\n:\nStudents take part in the seminars, workshops, group discussion and also submit assignment in different topics prescribed in syllabus.Special attention is given to the slow learner.\nMr. Biswajit Bora\nAssistant Professor\nhttps://publish.melamoracollege.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/BISWAJIT-BORA-PROFILE.pptx\nMrs Pollavi Saikia\nAssistant Professor\nMrs Swapnali Borah\nAssistant Professor\nOLD FACULTIES DETAILS:\nName: Mr. Tarun Saikia\nMrs. Poonam Singha Boruah.\nTEACHING\nMETHOD :\nTraditional lecture method\nBy doing question-answer session\nSpecial & tutorial classes\nWEAKNESS :\nFinancial help is needed for digitalization of the Department. Lack of enough ICT facilities.\nOPPORTUNITIES:\nWide scope for the students to build up their career.\nScope for the vast teaching experience & improvement of teaching for faculty members.\nCHALLENGES :\nICT tools needed for covering 50% classes as e-learning to cope with the NEP,2020.\nFUTURE PLAN :\nT\nhe main objective of the department is to provide maximum number of good students and encourage them to higher education. Faculty members are also dedicated in this process. The primary aim of the department is to develop the basic concept of morality among students so that they would become a good & socially responsible citizen in future.\nUSEFUL LINKS\nIGNOU\nUniversity Grant Commission\nGetting to NAAC\nDirectorate Of Higher Education\nGuwahati University\nDibrugarh University\nOTHER LINKS\nIQAC\nALUMNI\nRTI\nOUR ADDRESS\nMelamora College\nMelamora Gaon, Golaghat\nAssam – 785621\nemail: admin@melamoracollege.com\nGallery\n© 2026 MELAMORA COLLEGE. All Rights Reserved. Designed by www.gkd619.com\nClose\nFont Resize\nA-\nA+\nKeyboard navigation\nReadable Font\nContrast\nChoose color\nblack\nwhite\ngreen\nblue\nred\norange\nyellow\nnavi\nUnderline links\nClear cookies\nImages Greyscale\nInvert Colors\nRemove Animations\nLights Off\nClose\nAccessibility by WAH\n1 st CYCLE SSR\n1.1\n1.1.1\n1.1.1\n1.3\n1.3\n1.3.2\n1.4\n2.1.1\n2.3\n2.3.1\n2.5\n2.6\n3.2\n3.4\n3.4.3\n3.5\n4.1\n4.2\n4.3\n5.1\n5.1.2\n5.4\n6.1\n6.2\n6.3\n6.3\n6.4\n6.5\n6.5.2\n7.1\n7.1\n7.2\n7.3\nAbout us\nAcademic Achievements\nAcademic calender\nAchievements\nAction Taken Report\nADD-ON COURSE\nAdmission closed\nADMISSION FORM 3RD SEMESTER\nADMISSION FORM 5TH SEMESTER\nAdmission Notice 2022-2023\nAdmission Notice for BA 3rd sem & 5th sem\nADMISSION PROCEDURE\nAlumni\nAlumni\nAnti Ragging Committee\nAQAR\nB.A 1st Semester (FYUGP) 2024-25 Session\nBest practice\nCells And Committees\nCertificate Programs\nCLASS ROUTINE\nCode of conduct:\nCollege Magazine\nComposition, minutes of the meetings of Statutory committees and Cells\nComputer Educations\nConstitution of the Melamora College Student’s union\nContact us\nCore Values\nCOURSE\nCourses\nDepartment of Assamese\nDepartment of Education\nDepartment of English\nDepartment of History\nDepartment of Philosophy\nDepartment of Political Science\nDepartment of Political Science\nDepartment of Sociology\